{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050246-silver-ladder-ladder-of-existence-bardoi-problem","id":1050246,"title":"[Silver Ladder] Ladder of Existence - Bardoi Problem","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-16T19:29:10-08:00","id":1050246,"title":"[Silver Ladder] Ladder of Existence - Bardoi Problem","content":"Rereading <b>Silver Ladder</b> Order book I have one massive problem \u2013 Great Ladder of Existence itself. And particularly it\u2019s priorities in eyes of Order. Quick recap for all \u2013 Silver Ladder believes there are classes for more essential strata\u2019s of society \u2013 those parts that <i>should </i>rule humanity at large. It\u2019s their titular Silver Ladder of Existence and it looks like this ( from top to down ):<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Mages</li> <li>Hiereoi \u2013 Philosophers and priests</li> <li>Technoi \u2013 Experts and specialists, modern examples are IT guys or architects</li> <li>Polemarchs \u2013 Managers and directors</li> <li>Stratiotoi \u2013 Mob enforcers, cops, soldier</li> <li>Bardoi \u2013 Movie stars, musicians and socialites</li> <li>Demoi \u2013 Simple crowd - laborers, service workers, the homeless and middle managers</li> <li>Terata \u2013 Monsters, like vampires, werewolves or changelings</li> </ol>I look over this list and I\u2019m really confused by Silver Ladder views. Especially on Bardoi \u2013 it\u2019s like third of character concepts connected to Order I think comes from \u2018secretly inspiring artists or singer\u2019 idea that fit so perfect Silver Ladder being <b><i>Voice</i></b> of Dragon. Them being lower than Stratiotoi, police and soldiers just sound - please forgive me, but\u2026 stupid?<br /> <br /> Bardoi works to inspire people, to remember them that they are <i>persons</i>, not cogs in machine, to look beyond their everyday worries and move their souls \u2013 it\u2019s like half of Elemental Percepts rights there! From my reading of Great Ladder, it should be that Bardoi be <b><i>on top</i></b> of Polemarchs, not <i>under</i> Stratiotoi, as they are more essential to Tearchs goals of freeing humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T19:35:17-08:00","id":1050254,"title":"","content":"<b>Bonus</b> - Example on what can Bardoi Tearch inspire in young witches ( with good music from <b>American Horror Story - Coven</b> ). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yT_vx6fPIoM\" data-code=\"yT_vx6fPIoM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/yT_vx6fPIoM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-16-2017, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T20:12:11-08:00","id":1050280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050246-silver-ladder-ladder-of-existence-bardoi-problem#post1050246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bardoi works to inspire people, to remember them that they are <i>persons</i>, not cogs in machine, to look beyond their everyday worries and move their souls \u2013 it\u2019s like half of Elemental Percepts rights there! From my reading of Great Ladder, it should be that Bardoi be <b><i>on top</i></b> of Polemarchs, not <i>under</i> Stratiotoi, as they are more essential to Tearchs goals of freeing humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally the first thing the section tells you about the placement of the Bardoi is that they're only important because they're famous <i>for any reason at all</i>. The latest viral video star doesn't need to have a shred of talent to be counted among the Bardoi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T21:07:37-08:00","id":1050308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Mages</li> <li>Hiereoi \u2013 Philosophers and priests</li> <li>Technoi \u2013 Experts and specialists, modern examples are IT guys or architects</li> <li>Polemarchs \u2013 Managers and directors</li> <li>Stratiotoi \u2013 Mob enforcers, cops, soldier</li> <li>Bardoi \u2013 Movie stars, musicians and socialites</li> <li>Demoi \u2013 Simple crowd - laborers, service workers, the homeless and middle managers</li> <li>Terata \u2013 Monsters, like vampires, werewolves or changelings</li> </ol> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bardoi works to inspire people, to remember them that they are <i>persons</i>, not cogs in machine, to look beyond their everyday worries and move their souls \u2013 it\u2019s like half of Elemental Percepts rights there! From my reading of Great Ladder, it should be that Bardoi be <b><i>on top</i></b> of Polemarchs, not <i>under</i> Stratiotoi, as they are more essential to Tearchs goals of freeing humanity. </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, Bardoi is not a catch-all category for artists. Those who have artistic talent in inspiring people as you describe above, those who create not mere earworms or viral videos but true masterpieces, easily qualify as Technoi in the sense that they're the experts and specialists of the art of inspiration. If those people develop a philosophy on art and life over a life-long career of pursuing Beauty, then they could qualify even as Hiereoi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T00:31:19-08:00","id":1050352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050246-silver-ladder-ladder-of-existence-bardoi-problem?p=1050308#post1050308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, Bardoi is not a catch-all category for artists. Those who have artistic talent in inspiring people as you describe above, those who create not mere earworms or viral videos but true masterpieces, easily qualify as Technoi in the sense that they're the experts and specialists of the art of inspiration. If those people develop a philosophy on art and life over a life-long career of pursuing Beauty, then they could qualify even as Hiereoi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, with those interpretation I can go on - even if this is not obvious from reading of Ladder of Existence section.<br /> <br /> Other interesting problem - I now read <i>Fallen Blossoms</i> Dark Era in Edo shoguante of Japan. In that time, society hierarchy was called Four Divisions of Society (<i>shinokosho</i>) and looked like this:<br /> <br /> 1. Samurai ( and informally priests and monks )<br /> 2. Farmers<br /> 3. Marchants<br /> 4. Eta ( 'No people', like proffesions on contact with death, childbirth, menstruation,<br /> disease, and other \u201cunclean\u201d activities )<br /> 5. Hinin ( like convicts and vagrants )<br /> 6. Other ( those totally outside of social order - like geisha and entertainers )<br /> <br /> <b>I wonder if Edo period Silver Ladder would follow their Western Ladder of Existence or rather stay to their homeland shogunate order of society?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-17-2017, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T02:05:35-08:00","id":1050378,"title":"","content":"You missed out artisans.<br /> <br /> It's possible, though bear in mind, it's an adaptation of an older Confusian model so I'd expect them to think of the catagories in more abstract terms rather than rigid caste hierarchy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T02:09:06-08:00","id":1050380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050246-silver-ladder-ladder-of-existence-bardoi-problem?p=1050352#post1050352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Other interesting problem - I now read <i>Fallen Blossoms</i> Dark Era in Edo shoguante of Japan. In that time, society hierarchy was called Four Divisions of Society (<i>shinokosho</i>) and looked like this:<br /> <br /> 1. Samurai ( and informally priests and monks )<br /> 2. Farmers<br /> 3. Marchants<br /> 4. Eta ( 'No people', like proffesions on contact with death, childbirth, menstruation,<br /> disease, and other \u201cunclean\u201d activities )<br /> 5. Hinin ( like convicts and vagrants )<br /> 6. Other ( those totally outside of social order - like geisha and entertainers )<br /> <br /> <b>I wonder if Edo period Silver Ladder would follow their Western Ladder of Existence or rather stay to their homeland shogunate order of society?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Most swordsmen would be Stratiatoi at best. Most samurai, being feudalists, would be Polemarchs who manage their piece of land and their family. The most skilled of those samurai, be in swordsmanship or politics (as in, managing their land) would be Technoi. And the rare few who actually understood and internalized the Buddhist/Shinto philosophy behind <i>bushido </i>(which was in reality not kept that well, despite how the modern era romanticizes it) would be Hiereoi.<br /> <br /> Merchants would be Polemarchs at best and never Technoi or above, since commerce wouldn't be recognized as an area of expertise or something to develop a philosophy upon until capitalism is fully fleshed out. Everyone else is mostly Demoi. Still, it's amusing that the entertainers would technically be Bardoi, placing them above most of the common folk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T09:58:41-08:00","id":1050557,"title":"","content":"I don't put too much stock on 1e order books since I feel all the orders have changed their focus significantly. I personally feel this ladder to be pretty ludicrous, and don't think many modern mages would put too much stock into it. Yeah, some might. But not enough to make it a core tenet of the Order.<br /> <br /> I belive 2e Silver Ladder to be more concerned with organizing and leading Mages, and leaving the specifics of managing Sleepers to retainers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T10:56:01-08:00","id":1050588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050246-silver-ladder-ladder-of-existence-bardoi-problem?p=1050557#post1050557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I belive 2e Silver Ladder to be more concerned with organizing and leading Mages, and leaving the specifics of managing Sleepers to retainers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see you didn't bother to read the entire 2e SL section, particularly the part about the Elemental Precepts and what the Star means to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T11:42:20-08:00","id":1050621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050246-silver-ladder-ladder-of-existence-bardoi-problem?p=1050557#post1050557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't put too much stock on 1e order books since I feel all the orders have changed their focus significantly. I personally feel this ladder to be pretty ludicrous, and don't think many modern mages would put too much stock into it. Yeah, some might. But not enough to make it a core tenet of the Order.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050246-silver-ladder-ladder-of-existence-bardoi-problem?p=1050588#post1050588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see you didn't bother to read the entire 2e SL section, particularly the part about the Elemental Precepts and what the Star means to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not too mention <b>Dark Eras</b> based on Silver Ladder points on leading everyone in their pointed hierarchy based on Sacred Trees or hierarchy of Heavens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T12:13:39-08:00","id":1050644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050246-silver-ladder-ladder-of-existence-bardoi-problem?p=1050588#post1050588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see you didn't bother to read the entire 2e SL section, particularly the part about the Elemental Precepts and what the Star means to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nowhere in the single parragraph dedicated to Star says anything about this outdated nonsense. Yes, the idea of a Ladder and that everyone has a place on it is there, but it's not this caste system bs. This very specific, rigid hierarchical and baseless order is a very tough sell to a modern person. And I wouldn't consider it a core tenet of the order anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T13:09:21-08:00","id":1050672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050246-silver-ladder-ladder-of-existence-bardoi-problem?p=1050644#post1050644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nowhere in the single parragraph dedicated to Star says anything about this outdated nonsense. Yes, the idea of a Ladder and that everyone has a place on it is there, but it's not this caste system bs. This very specific, rigid hierarchical and baseless order is a very tough sell to a modern person. And I wouldn't consider it a core tenet of the order anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>The caste system isn't rigid, it's about defining where a person is on the ladder and then pushing them up it (at their own pace) until everyone is at the top. So yeah, it still applies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T17:06:33-08:00","id":1050802,"title":"","content":"I think the contradiction is that although Silver Ladder are posing as altruistic idealists, their hierarchy system reveals a more arrogant side of them.<br /> <br /> Silver Ladder is like a University, with it's (Mage) members being the professors and students being Sleepers.<br /> <br /> All professors know that their job is to elevate their students towards some degree of higher knowledge. (All are Silver Ladder)<br /> Some professors believe that <b>each</b> student should recieve equivalent amounts of education thus helping the weak students more. (Ladder's Equality-for-all Ideal)<br /> Others believe that because students learn at different rates, so different speed classes are needed, thus helping the strong students more. (Ladder's hierarchy system)<br /> But most are somewhere in between<br /> <br /> Maybe there are multiple Silver Ladders of Existance, different for each Caucus/Mentor/Member, with the book describing the dominant one.<br /> Maybe Bardoi are higher Polemarchs in the Silver Ladder of Paris , where offsprings from notable musicians and artists become Sleepwalkers.<br /> <br /> Sadly, I do not have the specific book, but does it say explicitly that there is only one Ladder of Existance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T19:55:45-08:00","id":1050860,"title":"","content":"The Silver Ladder book says that, no, this model of the Ladder is not the only one, merely the dominant one. Local variation and heresy are pretty much the rule rather than the exception for the Pentacle Orders.<br /> <br /> I don't see the Ladder's attitudes as a contradiction, though, myself; they're noblesse oblige incarnate. That arrogance isn't a bug, it's a feature. Back at the turn of the last century, they'd be a target for Kipling's satire. There's no logical contradiction to it, merely a great moral dubiousness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T21:06:14-08:00","id":1050874,"title":"","content":"Shadowjim, I very like University metaphor. It's exactly how it is in modern higher education and that's why I always felt that 'university cabals' should be made rather from Silver Ladder than Mysterium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T21:32:57-08:00","id":1050880,"title":"","content":"Yes, because if there's any place to acquire extreme wealth and political power, it's pursuing a career in academia!<br /> <br /> No, I'm not bitter, you're bitter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T02:54:39-08:00","id":1050923,"title":"","content":"I get the impression that the ladder is still a part of the 2e SL. Dave Brookshaw has referred to it at least once I can remember in recent times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T05:10:33-08:00","id":1050954,"title":"","content":"More than once, but yes. Its come up in reference to 2e, so its very much relevant unless the ST decides to drop it. From what I understand, 2e is an attempt to update all the changes that the Orders went through in 1e into a single core book. That includes the evolution of the Ladder and its philosophies. The hiearchy thus given is actually one of the evolved pieces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T10:24:49-08:00","id":1051049,"title":"","content":"I see it more as the Ladder listing the Bardoi as base, pointless entertainers who serve no purpose beyond distracting the populace as opposed to using their craft to enlighten them.<br /> \u200bThink of it as comparing Shakespeare to reality TV. \u200bIn their eyes the truly good ones would qualify as philosophers and priests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 02-18-2017, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T10:45:35-08:00","id":1051060,"title":"","content":"Yeah, an actor, playwright, singer, etc., who uses their medium to convey an active philosophy in an attempt to uplift humanity and guide them to something better would be a Hiereos. Bardoi are people whose sole contribution is in making something pretty. A good actor may indeed be someone of real skill and ability, but if all they're doing is telling someone else's story, the Ladder doesn't consider them that valuable; they're not really masters of their own fate nor guides of any sort to others.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter, in other words, if a singer can give people goosebumps with their rendition of Handel's Glory to God (not really a solo piece, I know, but not the point); it's <i>Handel</i> who captured that beauty and ideal in the first place and put it to paper. Handel would be a Technos, the performers merely Bardoi.<br /> <br /> It's not the medium that matters, in other words, but what the person brings to others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:10:05-08:00","id":1052090,"title":"","content":"That's something I can agree to. I just want to add that some philosophers (I think Plato) considered the &quot;admiration of beautiful things&quot; an ideal in itself. The reasoning behind this is that beauty reminds to the person (that recognized it) that perfection still exists in this world of Forms and Ideas. On the other hand, maybe it's just me being a Bardos (singular of Bardoi), trying to secure a higher level in the Ladder of Things :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:30:42-08:00","id":1052109,"title":"","content":"The Greeks definitely had an idea that virtue could be tangible, yeah. Virtue wasn't just some abstract ideal, it was how close to perfection something came. Being beautiful was considered virtuous, just as being ugly was considered a sign that apparently the gods just didn't love you. When people believe that today, we call it prosperity theology.<br /> <br /> The Ladder, though, doesn't believe the whims of capricious gods should be given much merit, though, so it seems like they'd probably err towards samsara; where whatever physical virtues you may have are treated as a pure luck that comes from blindly wandering from incarnation to incarnation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:41:12-08:00","id":1052117,"title":"","content":"from Plato's Republic in wikipedia-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Concluding a theme brought up most explicitly in the Analogies of the Sun and Divided Line in Book VI, Socrates finally rejects any form of imitative art and concludes that such artists have no place in the just city. He continues on to argue for the immortality of the psyche and even espouses a theory of reincarnation. He finishes by detailing the rewards of being just, both in this life and the next. Artists create things but they are only different copies of the idea of the original. &quot;And whenever any one informs us that he has found a man who knows all the arts, and all things else that anybody knows, and every single thing with a higher degree of accuracy than any other man \u2014 whoever tells us this, I think that we can only imagine to be a simple creature who is likely to have been deceived by some wizard or actor whom he met, and whom he thought all-knowing, because he himself was unable to analyze the nature of knowledge and ignorance and imitation.&quot;</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> as far as I'm seeing it, the Ladder of Things pretty much corresponds to the ideals of Platonic philosophy- my sister has learned about it in her degree, so she may know more about it, but I do remember that according to Plato, artists are found near the bottom of the world in spiritual means, as they never truly make, only imitate the world around it, and by doing that he steps away from the Idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T13:05:14-08:00","id":1052130,"title":"","content":"But 'artist' actors or singers, <i>creating</i> their art, are still Hiereos in the eyes of Tearchs? They are 'heroes' of Fallen World, giving people way to connect with Ideal and seeing past the Lie?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T13:07:13-08:00","id":1052136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050246-silver-ladder-ladder-of-existence-bardoi-problem?p=1052130#post1052130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But 'artist' actors or singers, <i>creating</i> their art, are still Hiereos in the eyes of Tearchs? They are 'heroes' of Fallen World, giving people way to connect with Ideal and seeing past the Lie?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably depends if you think they're any good.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T13:39:55-08:00","id":1052162,"title":"","content":"When readin <b>Cinder</b>'s materials for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1047206-fanmade-dark-era-beast-geist-the-forest-that-weeps/\">Congo Free State Dark Era</a> I suddenly come to see how Ladder of Existence can be seen as truly bad thing from outside of Silver Ladder perspective. Just see this paragraph on missionaries...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Fundamentalists and racist missionaries do exist, but most of those who come to Congo sincerely do so with the purpose of helping the locals. That is, according to their perspective, taking them out of the jungle, teaching them how to read and write and making them abandon their previous lifestyle to embrace those of the Westerners. While also making them convert, of course. It\u2019s questionable, but they do mean well: in their eyes the wonders of the Western civilization and technology can only do good and to convert an African means to save his soul. One can argue that many of those helped by missionaries come to live a better life indeed. As mentioned before, it\u2019s from the missionaries that most of the denounces against Leopold\u2019s regime come.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I just can't stop to think that's exactly how Silver Ladder mages would look on the all Nameless around them - and this 'missionary complex' would be one of great reasons why Nameless reformed in to Free Council in the first place <i>against</i> Ladder. <br /> <br /> And now I cannot to stop think about Silver Ladder lead mission or conquistadors expedition in Age of Discovery that Tearchs want's locals ' to embrace true Atlantean heritage', whenever they can go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T14:08:28-08:00","id":1052176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050246-silver-ladder-ladder-of-existence-bardoi-problem?p=1052130#post1052130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But 'artist' actors or singers, <i>creating</i> their art, are still Hiereos in the eyes of Tearchs? They are 'heroes' of Fallen World, giving people way to connect with Ideal and seeing past the Lie?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Platonicaly&quot; speaking, it doesn't matter. They are still making art- and art only mimics, not creates. It is about discussing what &quot;art&quot; truly means, and in the eyes of classical Platonic view (as far as I understand it), the act of art is a lesser one. Art never truly make, only copy, and by acting as if it creates when it doesn't is what places artists so low in the Platonic &quot;social order&quot;. &quot;Inspiring people to see the truth through art&quot; is not, as far as I'm aware, a part of the Platonic philosophy- as inspiring the masses is the role of philosophers. The world view of the Silver Ladder in that context is strongly based around Plato's paradigm, including considering soldiers and their like as more important to society than artists.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not saying that artists inspiring people to see beyond the Lie is not a good concept- only that it is not a part of the Platonic philosophy (as far as I'm aware- again, I study chemistry, not philosophy), and if the Silver Ladder were to base itself strongly around Platonic ideals, than it would not accept artists as having an high place in the social order. It is a matter of a world view- and I imagine that even in the Silver Ladder itself there are discussions and disagreements about how truly is that social order is valid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T14:22:04-08:00","id":1052183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050246-silver-ladder-ladder-of-existence-bardoi-problem?p=1052176#post1052176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are still making art- and art only mimics, not creates.</div> </div> </div> </div>T<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">hat's only true of imitative art. Plato/Socrates has other reasons for disliking poetry which I believe are roughly that it's not terribly well thought out. Everyone loves Homer (including it seems Socrates) but no one gives much consideration to what kind of ideas that teaches.</span></span><br /> <br /> Bear in mind, Plato has no problems with creating false mythologies and lies if it serves a proper purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T14:47:31-08:00","id":1052202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050246-silver-ladder-ladder-of-existence-bardoi-problem?p=1052183#post1052183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> T<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">hat's only true of imitative art. Plato/Socrates has other reasons for disliking poetry which I believe are roughly that it's not terribly well thought out. Everyone loves Homer (including it seems Socrates) but no one gives much consideration to what kind of ideas that teaches.</span></span><br /> <br /> Bear in mind, Plato has no problems with creating false mythologies and lies if it serves a proper purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>like I've said- I'm not a philosophy specialist. The only reason I know that fact is because my sister had a degree at visual arts, after all :P Anyway, it still seems to be the base for why the Bardoi were placed so low in the Ladder- even if what they do inspires others, they don't do that to inspire. A philosopher who happens to use art is different from a artist who happens to make philosophy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T15:00:37-08:00","id":1052210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1050246-silver-ladder-ladder-of-existence-bardoi-problem?p=1052162#post1052162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When readin <b>Cinder</b>'s materials for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1047206-fanmade-dark-era-beast-geist-the-forest-that-weeps/\">Congo Free State Dark Era</a> I suddenly come to see how Ladder of Existence can be seen as truly bad thing from outside of Silver Ladder perspective. Just see this paragraph on missionaries...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I just can't stop to think that's exactly how Silver Ladder mages would look on the all Nameless around them - and this 'missionary complex' would be one of great reasons why Nameless reformed in to Free Council in the first place <i>against</i> Ladder.<br /> <br /> And now I cannot to stop think about Silver Ladder lead mission or conquistadors expedition in Age of Discovery that Tearchs want's locals ' to embrace true Atlantean heritage', whenever they can go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's pretty much what happens when the thearchs get Hubristic; mistaking their role for Rulers, when they should be Leaders. Every Order has their dark side, and this is the Ladder's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T15:41:08-08:00","id":1052236,"title":"","content":"Every group and age falls victim to ethnocentricity, the belief that their ways and values are best, if they didn't then they would change to something else. Hubris happens when they decide that others should do as they do and the benefits justify using coercion and outright force to make it happen.<br /> \u200bMages would be no exception with most of their ideas originating around the Mediterranean and northern Europe.<br /> This I think would be the primary reason behind the Free Council and the Nameless War, made up of those who don't share those ways and values and resist changing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}